<title>SWITZERLAND: BOE's Davies says EMU not weakening London City.</title>
<headline>BOE's Davies says EMU not weakening London City.</headline>
<dateline>DAVOS, Switzerland 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England deputy governor Howard Davies said on Friday uncertainties about European Union plans for Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) were not weakening London as a financial centre.</p>
<p>&quot;So far, the uncertainty about EMU has not had any serious effect on the City of London,&quot; he told reporters at the World Economic Forum in Davos.</p>
<p>Davies said the City was in fact gaining strength as a financial centre.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment, the movement of financial institutions tend to be the other way. London seems to be strengthening its position as a financial centre,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Davos Newsroom, +41-81-413 1449</p>
</text>
